WEBVTT

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:03.770
Chiri!

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:06.940
The final Divine Idol Grand Prix draws near,

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:10.530
yet you haven't found suitable team members.

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:12.070
This won't do.

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:13.780
Yes...

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:16.240
We have to do something, and quickly...

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:22.210
Something smells sweet! Licky-lick!

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:24.920
Pepper?

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:27.600
Can eat for dessert?

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:29.170
No, you cannot!

00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:30.150
Licky-licky...

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:32.640
Everyone raised these flowers together!
Licky-licky...

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:34.030
Together?

00:00:34.030 --> 00:00:36.340
Though some flowers haven't bloomed yet...

00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:38.760
Just like me.

00:00:39.610 --> 00:00:42.680
I really want to win the next Grand Prix,

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:45.270
but without a team, I'm just a little bud.

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:48.180
When will I ever manage to bloom?

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:51.870
<i>I've prepared myself for this-ucha.</i>

00:00:51.870 --> 00:00:54.240
<i>I give you permission to eat me-ucha!</i>

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:57.120
But if Usacha's that sure about it...

00:00:57.120 --> 00:00:58.680
I've gotta do my best as well–

00:00:59.280 --> 00:00:59.950
Pepper, no!

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:03.910
<i>Just wait, Usacha. I'm not going to give up!</i>

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:43.970
Chiri-chan!

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:48.120
Non-chan. Has something suddenly come up?

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:51.850
Hello to you too, Janice.

00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:53.150
Hello.

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:54.980
For true friendship...

00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:55.940
Licky-stick!

00:02:56.760 --> 00:02:57.900
Unclean!

00:02:59.110 --> 00:02:59.520
Tsukikawa

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:03.340
Chiri-shan, chiri-shan, chiri-shan, chiri-shan-shan!

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:06.450
So she can do her water dance outside of PriPara, too..

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:07.160
Licky-stick!
Chiri-shan, chiri-shan, chiri-shan, chiri-shan-shan!

00:03:07.690 --> 00:03:09.160
Pepper! Heel!

00:03:11.070 --> 00:03:14.380
Don't worry, Chiri. I won't let Pepper lick you today.

00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:16.250
I'll keep her at a safe distance.

00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:17.960
Do you hear me, Pepper?

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:21.130
Loud and clear. Listen to Boss!

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:22.430
See? Please?

00:03:22.430 --> 00:03:23.830
Will you listen to us?

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:25.470
Chiri.

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:29.100
Are these ladies your friends?

00:03:29.830 --> 00:03:32.100
Father! Oh, they're just...

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:37.860
Garlic! Garlic!

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:41.500
Well, I <i>was</i> just eating gyoza... is there a problem?

00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:44.030
No garlic! Garlic stink!

00:03:46.270 --> 00:03:48.700
We're so sorry, Mr Chiri's father!

00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:53.420
Your friends certainly are in high spirits.

00:03:56.210 --> 00:03:59.230
Chiri, your dad's really a nice guy.

00:03:59.230 --> 00:04:01.260
O–Oh, is he?

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:02.930
No running!

00:04:02.930 --> 00:04:04.790
Ooh, shiny!

00:04:08.150 --> 00:04:10.980
So slippery! Can't grip with toenails!

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:16.610
Um, you can walk if you shuffle along...

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:18.610
That's Chiri for you!

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:20.650
How fearsome!

00:04:21.830 --> 00:04:24.290
Wow! The garden's huge as well!

00:04:24.290 --> 00:04:25.870
Sapanna even more huge!

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:28.860
<i>Nothing's</i> big compared to a whole country!

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:34.580
<i>Okay! I think we can talk properly today!</i>

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:40.050
Um, so I was thinking... Let's give what Usacha said a shot!

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:43.480
<i>These three are rock-paper-scissors-ucha!</i>

00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:47.760
<i>No matter what rival they face,
they can throw the winning move-ucha!</i>

00:04:48.190 --> 00:04:49.600
Isn't that amazing?

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:54.960
It's because we're so different that our potential is limitless.

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:57.690
I'm sure we can win the Grand Prix as well!

00:04:57.690 --> 00:05:00.110
With teammates of <i>this</i> level?

00:05:00.350 --> 00:05:01.800
Oh, but...

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:04.020
Look, Pepper's totally into the idea.

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:05.790
Eat Usacha!

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:10.340
Now we just need you to decide, too.

00:05:13.340 --> 00:05:15.300
Can eat that flower?

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:18.040
No! No, it's impossible!

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:22.450
I just can't handle Pepper at all...

00:05:22.450 --> 00:05:24.760
Chiri! What do you think you're doing?

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:27.840
It's time for flower arrangement.

00:05:29.270 --> 00:05:30.850
Certainly, Grandmother.

00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:35.850
Oh, but Grandmother, today
Chiri's lovely friends are visiting...

00:05:35.850 --> 00:05:37.560
Can't we hold off a little...

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:39.840
Be silent!

00:05:43.880 --> 00:05:46.320
The Tsukikawa Family's history spans three hundred years.

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:49.320
Known as a master of the flower arranging arts.

00:05:49.880 --> 00:05:55.910
As the heir to the Tsukikawa family,
flower arrangement takes precedence over all.

00:05:55.910 --> 00:05:58.710
But surely that can wait until her friends–

00:05:58.710 --> 00:06:01.170
Are you still prattling?

00:06:06.060 --> 00:06:08.300
But why?

00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:10.510
Icy poles! Look tasty!

00:06:10.910 --> 00:06:15.770
I approve, Chiri's grandmother.
There's no sense coddling then.

00:06:16.170 --> 00:06:18.980
That's how it's going to be. We'll be leaving now.

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:21.880
Chiri, come!

00:06:21.880 --> 00:06:23.940
Most certainly.

00:06:23.940 --> 00:06:26.780
Non icy pole so tasty!

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:29.860
H–Her grandma's a force to be reckoned with.

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:37.240
Thank you for your consideration.

00:06:39.990 --> 00:06:41.000
Next.

00:06:41.630 --> 00:06:42.420
Yes...

00:06:43.360 --> 00:06:48.100
If Chiri doesn't meet her grandmother's approval each day, she's not allowed outside?

00:06:49.130 --> 00:06:53.390
Chiri always tries her hardest,
but lately she seems somehow preoccupied.

00:06:53.390 --> 00:06:56.930
I'm worried she's hit some kind of wall...

00:06:56.930 --> 00:07:00.390
Preoccupied? With the team?

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:02.900
Spider-ider-ider-ider...

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:04.110
Spider.

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:20.500
Don't eat that!

00:07:20.950 --> 00:07:25.710
Chiri, you must overcome your entomophobia.

00:07:25.710 --> 00:07:27.670
Y–Yes...

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:32.060
Then call me when you have produced something satisfactory.

00:07:32.060 --> 00:07:33.700
You're not to leave...

00:07:34.380 --> 00:07:38.100
until you can complete one work a day!

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:40.140
U–Understood...

00:07:42.490 --> 00:07:43.600
Chiri!

00:07:44.570 --> 00:07:49.860
I've brought your friends before your grandmother returns.

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:50.800
Toodles.

00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:52.730
Thank you very much.

00:07:54.490 --> 00:07:56.410
I was thinking...

00:07:56.410 --> 00:07:59.950
The way you turn so high-handed in PriPara –

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:03.210
is it a way of dealing with things in your everyday life?

00:08:03.210 --> 00:08:06.590
What? Um, I don't really know about that...

00:08:06.590 --> 00:08:09.380
Jeez, you can't just spit it out!

00:08:13.230 --> 00:08:16.050
Now we just need to decide the team's name,

00:08:16.050 --> 00:08:19.090
and I can depart this world without regrets-ucha!

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:21.520
So anyway,

00:08:21.850 --> 00:08:24.280
returning to our discussion before,

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:29.940
I really want to try hard for Usacha's sake, and form a team with you!

00:08:29.940 --> 00:08:32.060
O–Oh, but I...

00:08:32.060 --> 00:08:37.540
But <i>first</i>, we need to get you to PriPara,
so we'll help you with your flower arrangement!

00:08:37.540 --> 00:08:39.300
Y–You will?

00:08:39.300 --> 00:08:40.490
Was tasty!

00:08:40.490 --> 00:08:42.220
Licky-gulp!

00:08:43.440 --> 00:08:45.460
Oh, my goodness!

00:08:45.460 --> 00:08:48.880
I can't complete an arrangement without any flowers!

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:51.740
She's ruined everything!

00:08:51.740 --> 00:08:52.700
Licky-gulp!

00:08:55.190 --> 00:08:57.760
Grandmother will be furious...

00:08:58.190 --> 00:09:01.230
What can we do if there aren't any flowers?

00:09:01.230 --> 00:09:05.700
She'll be so... She'll be so...

00:09:05.700 --> 00:09:07.560
By the way, what's that over there?

00:09:07.560 --> 00:09:08.900
It's a greenhouse...

00:09:08.900 --> 00:09:10.480
Ooh-ooh! Can eat?

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:12.350
A greenhouse?

00:09:12.350 --> 00:09:15.860
That's it! A greenhouse has got to have tons of flowers!

00:09:19.430 --> 00:09:22.630
Incredible! They're all so lovely!

00:09:23.640 --> 00:09:30.370
But Grandmother ordered those flowers specially for today's practice...

00:09:30.370 --> 00:09:32.300
I don't think we have the same ones...

00:09:32.300 --> 00:09:36.100
Then why don't you pick your own and arrange them as you wish?

00:09:36.100 --> 00:09:37.430
Oh, but...

00:09:37.870 --> 00:09:43.430
I kind of felt your arrangement was stiff.

00:09:45.800 --> 00:09:50.040
You know, I'm the Animal and Flower Caretaker at my school.

00:09:51.190 --> 00:09:55.350
I sometimes think, when I'm watering...

00:09:56.950 --> 00:09:59.340
Maybe flowers grown in a greenhouse...

00:10:00.790 --> 00:10:07.340
would like to experience a wider world when it's time to be picked.

00:10:11.030 --> 00:10:13.960
But flowers outside have hard time.

00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:14.670
What?

00:10:14.970 --> 00:10:19.090
Once in Sapanna, no rain for a long time.

00:10:26.950 --> 00:10:28.520
<i>Dance!</i>

00:10:29.380 --> 00:10:34.480
Everyone did rain dance for many days.

00:10:35.800 --> 00:10:38.820
<i>Ooh-ooh! Ooh-ooh!</i>

00:10:47.380 --> 00:10:49.550
But they all fell down.

00:10:49.550 --> 00:10:51.640
Oh, how awful.

00:10:53.120 --> 00:10:54.500
That time...

00:10:55.450 --> 00:10:59.200
One flower, received everyone's feelings.

00:11:10.940 --> 00:11:13.400
<i>Hooray!</i>

00:11:13.400 --> 00:11:15.480
Sapanna came back to life!

00:11:16.590 --> 00:11:18.280
<i>Yahoo!</i>

00:11:19.240 --> 00:11:20.910
Am sure that rain...

00:11:21.770 --> 00:11:24.720
Come from King Protia calling!

00:11:29.900 --> 00:11:31.550
How wonderful!

00:11:31.550 --> 00:11:33.810
That's an incredible story...

00:11:37.120 --> 00:11:39.670
King Protia!

00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:42.140
You really helped us that time!

00:11:42.860 --> 00:11:44.550
Ooh? What now?

00:11:46.810 --> 00:11:49.920
King Protia says "Take me!" to Chiri.

00:11:49.920 --> 00:11:50.890
Is that so?

00:11:51.520 --> 00:11:53.220
To me?

00:11:57.980 --> 00:11:59.550
It <i>is</i> pretty...

00:12:00.620 --> 00:12:04.070
It's vivid, and powerful...

00:12:05.630 --> 00:12:08.630
Flowers which turn towards the sun in order to bloom...

00:12:10.140 --> 00:12:14.560
Flowers which try their hardest to bloom, and help others...

00:12:16.720 --> 00:12:20.010
I've long wondered what thoughts flowers held...

00:12:24.650 --> 00:12:27.570
If the rain falls, the flowers can bloom.

00:12:27.570 --> 00:12:30.960
So if the flower blooms, rain can fall.

00:12:31.680 --> 00:12:32.930
I...

00:12:35.300 --> 00:12:36.510
I...

00:12:36.510 --> 00:12:38.480
I want to arrange this flower!

00:12:44.700 --> 00:12:47.960
It's a protia! Protia from that time!

00:12:47.960 --> 00:12:49.490
It's wonderful, Chiri!

00:12:52.580 --> 00:12:55.600
Th–The name of the piece is "A Prayer for Rain".

00:12:55.600 --> 00:12:58.420
I wanted to express the flowers' feelings.

00:12:58.420 --> 00:13:00.090
Thank you for your consideration.

00:13:04.430 --> 00:13:06.760
See, you can do it if you set your mind to it.

00:13:07.120 --> 00:13:08.250
Oh?

00:13:08.250 --> 00:13:12.220
The sublime sensation of energy, of looming over.

00:13:12.220 --> 00:13:15.730
The feeling of parched earth – I like it.

00:13:16.320 --> 00:13:17.650
You pass.

00:13:19.640 --> 00:13:21.650
Thank you so much!

00:13:21.650 --> 00:13:23.170
She did it!

00:13:23.170 --> 00:13:24.960
Thank you, Pepper!

00:13:25.670 --> 00:13:27.570
Thank you, Non!

00:13:30.900 --> 00:13:33.870
G–G–Grandmother...

00:13:33.870 --> 00:13:38.320
These two helped me complete that work.

00:13:38.320 --> 00:13:43.650
You see, Chiri? When we combine our powers, we can be the best team in all of PriPara!

00:13:43.650 --> 00:13:44.800
PriPara?

00:13:45.160 --> 00:13:48.930
Yes! I want to snap tickets for the formation ceremony now!

00:13:49.520 --> 00:13:52.600
Well, we've no time for any other options. Very well.

00:13:52.600 --> 00:13:54.390
I will not oppose this.

00:13:55.660 --> 00:13:57.800
Oh, thank you!

00:13:57.800 --> 00:14:01.290
Chiri! So you were going to PriPara?

00:14:01.290 --> 00:14:02.860
Y–Yes...

00:14:03.200 --> 00:14:06.850
My, oh, my. I had no idea.

00:14:08.110 --> 00:14:10.410
Non, you've done well-ucha!

00:14:10.410 --> 00:14:13.040
And I've decided on our team name, too-ucha!

00:14:13.990 --> 00:14:15.020
And that name...

00:14:15.020 --> 00:14:16.750
is NonSugar-ucha!

00:14:17.390 --> 00:14:18.990
NonSugar?

00:14:18.990 --> 00:14:20.490
You won't go down easy-ucha!

00:14:22.480 --> 00:14:23.500
Okay!

00:14:24.010 --> 00:14:26.560
All right! Let's get the team formation underway!

00:14:26.560 --> 00:14:27.510
Ooh-ooh!
Okay!

00:14:33.430 --> 00:14:35.850
Promise: believe in friendship.

00:14:37.250 --> 00:14:39.310
Rhythm: carved in our hearts.

00:14:40.290 --> 00:14:42.480
Paradise: our goal.

00:14:43.450 --> 00:14:46.780
We swear to stand on stage as one!

00:14:47.190 --> 00:14:49.150
Ucha!

00:14:51.450 --> 00:14:54.270
I won't let you forget that promise – let's go!

00:14:54.270 --> 00:14:55.490
Okay!

00:14:57.380 --> 00:14:59.290
Prostrate yourselves and capisce!

00:14:59.290 --> 00:15:01.210
As you will!

00:15:01.210 --> 00:15:04.890
I refuse to form a team with the likes of you two.

00:15:04.890 --> 00:15:06.380
Ucha?
What?

00:15:06.380 --> 00:15:09.300
Well, I can't say I didn't see this coming...

00:15:09.300 --> 00:15:11.010
You'll form this team, won't you?

00:15:11.010 --> 00:15:14.190
You just promised you would!

00:15:14.190 --> 00:15:17.070
I may well have, but I shan't join a team with these <i>commo</i>–

00:15:17.070 --> 00:15:21.230
Chiri! It is a violation of the rules to break a promise once made!

00:15:21.860 --> 00:15:25.070
The one thing I condemn above all!

00:15:25.070 --> 00:15:26.780
Like my sister!

00:15:28.100 --> 00:15:29.950
That's exactly right!

00:15:32.990 --> 00:15:33.990
Who?

00:15:33.990 --> 00:15:35.420
You wouldn't be...

00:15:38.530 --> 00:15:41.000
I am indeed. How do I look?

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:43.730
You youngsters won't eclipse my glamour just yet.

00:15:43.730 --> 00:15:45.230
Wow, amazing!

00:15:45.230 --> 00:15:48.630
You sure are lovely! Granny, you're the best!

00:15:48.630 --> 00:15:49.970
Why, thank you.

00:15:51.130 --> 00:15:53.800
Breaking a promise besmirches the Tsukikawa name.

00:15:53.800 --> 00:15:57.430
To say nothing of the pledge you made with that flower.

00:15:58.010 --> 00:15:59.720
Promises important!

00:16:00.390 --> 00:16:02.730
It has been a long time, Legendary One.

00:16:03.320 --> 00:16:07.110
None has been your match since the romantic Taisho period.

00:16:07.110 --> 00:16:08.380
Legendary One?

00:16:08.380 --> 00:16:09.990
From the Taisho period?

00:16:10.730 --> 00:16:15.820
Thank you, Meganii-san.
You've not changed at all since then, either.

00:16:16.410 --> 00:16:18.040
You're too kind.

00:16:18.310 --> 00:16:22.120
Very well. Henceforth, I, Tsukikawa Chiri,

00:16:22.120 --> 00:16:26.650
shall form a team with the two of you and claim victory in the Grand Prix!

00:16:26.650 --> 00:16:27.840
Ooh-ooh!
Okay!

00:16:38.100 --> 00:16:41.230
Scan the appropriate number of MyTickets for your coord.

00:16:41.230 --> 00:16:44.140
You can also scan each other's Friend Tickets.

00:16:44.690 --> 00:16:46.730
Starting the Coord Change.

00:16:49.600 --> 00:16:54.320
NonSugar's first team coord features darling, matching polka dots!

00:16:54.320 --> 00:16:56.740
NonSugar Girly Ribbon Coord!

00:16:56.740 --> 00:16:57.790
Non!

00:16:59.830 --> 00:17:05.500
Miss Non is sweet, Miss Chiri is elegant, and Miss Pepper is resplendent in fur!

00:17:05.500 --> 00:17:07.830
NonSugar Elegant Coord!

00:17:07.830 --> 00:17:08.990
Chiri!

00:17:11.190 --> 00:17:16.010
The coords express each member's
particularities – each like a self-introduction!

00:17:16.010 --> 00:17:18.970
NonSugar Soft Fur Coord!

00:17:18.970 --> 00:17:20.220
Ooh-ooh!

00:17:21.420 --> 00:17:23.320
It's their first team performance!

00:17:23.320 --> 00:17:25.100
Go for it, Non!

00:17:25.560 --> 00:17:27.480
My heart's in my throat-ucha!

00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:29.060
Do your utmost.

00:17:29.060 --> 00:17:31.020
NonSugar!

00:17:31.050 --> 00:17:32.540
Go for it!

00:17:32.540 --> 00:17:34.030
We're rooting for you!

00:18:48.940 --> 00:18:52.230
Making Drama, switch on!

00:18:56.890 --> 00:18:58.240
Sparkling!

00:18:59.400 --> 00:19:00.280
Chiri!

00:19:00.280 --> 00:19:01.160
Ooh-ooh!

00:19:01.160 --> 00:19:02.030
Tee-hee!

00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:04.990
One Thousand and One Nights.

00:19:10.490 --> 00:19:12.250
Secret...

00:19:19.580 --> 00:19:21.260
Refinement!

00:19:22.220 --> 00:19:24.350
Cyalume Change!

00:19:30.810 --> 00:19:31.020
Non!

00:19:31.020 --> 00:19:31.520
Chiri!

00:19:31.520 --> 00:19:32.540
Ooh-ooh!

00:20:06.620 --> 00:20:08.640
NonSugar's the best!

00:20:09.640 --> 00:20:14.320
NonSugar has ranked up in their
début performance – to Promising Idol!

00:20:14.320 --> 00:20:15.900
NonSugar, you're all so cute!

00:20:15.900 --> 00:20:17.050
Non-chan!

00:20:17.050 --> 00:20:18.710
Lady Chiri, you're simply wonderful!

00:20:22.750 --> 00:20:25.410
We didn't receive the Divine Idol Challenge?

00:20:25.800 --> 00:20:30.520
That coord was simply childish...
and Pepper looks like some beast!

00:20:30.520 --> 00:20:33.250
You're tripping me up!

00:20:33.250 --> 00:20:36.080
You all put on a wonderful performance-ucha!

00:20:36.080 --> 00:20:37.290
I'm so glad-ucha!

00:20:37.690 --> 00:20:39.800
Thanks, Usacha!

00:20:39.800 --> 00:20:43.390
But if we formed a team, then that means...

00:20:43.390 --> 00:20:44.590
Eat Usacha!

00:20:45.350 --> 00:20:47.070
Very well-ucha.

00:20:48.750 --> 00:20:49.770
Pepper.

00:20:50.700 --> 00:20:54.020
From now on, ensure you bathe and brush your teeth every day.

00:20:54.620 --> 00:20:57.260
Chiri will be cross with you less often,

00:20:57.260 --> 00:20:59.170
Non's efforts will be rewarded,

00:20:59.170 --> 00:21:01.990
and the team's bonds will be forever.

00:21:02.350 --> 00:21:03.690
Usacha...

00:21:04.230 --> 00:21:06.200
That's my wish-ucha!

00:21:07.030 --> 00:21:12.540
Your training regimen is laid out in here,
so you simply need to give it your all-ucha.

00:21:12.860 --> 00:21:16.460
A manager being eaten? This is totally unprecedented.

00:21:16.820 --> 00:21:20.280
Make sure you stay friends forever-ucha!

00:21:20.790 --> 00:21:21.760
Okay!

00:21:23.630 --> 00:21:25.880
Just hold on a second!

00:21:25.880 --> 00:21:29.260
You can eat her once we win the Grand Prix!

00:21:29.990 --> 00:21:33.230
I mean, um, you know...

00:21:33.230 --> 00:21:35.730
Usacha was eating garlic earlier, you know!

00:21:35.730 --> 00:21:37.730
G–Garlic?

00:21:37.730 --> 00:21:41.180
Yep! A big old bulb of garlic, like a pumpkin!

00:21:41.180 --> 00:21:43.070
She ate the whole thing right up!

00:21:44.220 --> 00:21:45.640
Gross!

00:21:45.640 --> 00:21:50.010
So hold off for now! The garlic smell won't disappear for a while!

00:21:50.890 --> 00:21:51.950
Non...

00:21:51.950 --> 00:21:54.080
It's fine; she can eat me...

00:21:54.080 --> 00:21:55.250
Of course she can't!

00:21:55.710 --> 00:21:59.000
That big bulb was like the king of garlic!

00:21:59.000 --> 00:22:00.380
Isn't that right, Pepper?

00:22:00.380 --> 00:22:01.750
Understand!

00:22:01.750 --> 00:22:05.200
Then when we win Grand Prix, no more garlic for Usacha!

00:22:05.200 --> 00:22:07.970
Got it! That works, doesn't it, Usacha?

00:22:08.440 --> 00:22:13.180
After all, we've got a lot left to do as a team!

00:22:13.180 --> 00:22:15.520
Okay-ucha!

00:22:16.150 --> 00:22:18.170
I think we're safe for now...

00:22:18.170 --> 00:22:19.240
Ucha!

00:23:50.920 --> 00:23:52.740
The time has cosmically arrived!

00:23:52.740 --> 00:23:55.850
At long last, we're start-intoretto!
Let's get fi-Renoir-ed up-Da Vinci!

00:23:55.850 --> 00:23:59.900
You'll be able to make PriPara coords from your own designs!

00:23:59.900 --> 00:24:03.630
And we'll be holding an out-of-the-cosmos
fashion show where the best coords compete!

00:24:03.630 --> 00:24:06.800
Come one, come all-assen!
We'll take any design-dro Botticelli you have!

00:24:06.800 --> 00:24:10.800
Show us what Utrillo can ser-zanne up!
Pabl-ish your artistic sense and Gogh for it;

00:24:10.800 --> 00:24:11.060
Get Gauguin, I say! Show Venus de Me-lo what you can do...

00:24:11.060 --> 00:24:13.800
Anyway, make sure you don't miss it!

00:24:13.800 --> 00:24:16.830
Next time, <i>Awaken! The Goddess's Dress Design</i>!

00:24:16.830 --> 00:24:19.850
Aim to be a Divine Idol! Let's go, PriPara!
